<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mago I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 550–530 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mago I was a Carthaginian leader of the sixth century BCE, active around 550 to 530 BCE, and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magonid-dynasty">Magonid dynasty</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s profile, he began the systematic empire-building that transformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> from a trading post into an imperial metropolis. He is associated with reforms of the Carthaginian army.</p></div>
